content.text:
I reviewed the diff against the full spec (Acceptance Criteria 1-6, Tasks 1-4, and Dev Notes) in `2-2-freie-sitzplaetze-auswaehlen.md`. Implementation closely tracks the spec's explicit code snippets for selection toggling (AC1/AC2), the belegt-guard on click and keyboard (AC3), roving-tabindex keyboard navigation with gang-skipping (AC4), the focus ring (AC5), and the client-only in-memory selection state with reset-on-route-reactivation (AC6). Tests cover the corresponding cases including the `Storage.prototype.setItem` negative test for AC6.

One deviation from the literal spec constraint found:

## Findings

- **`ersteSitzplatzPosition` scans all rows instead of only the first row (Task 3, subtask 1)**
  - Violates: Task 3 constraint — "auf die erste Sitzplatz-Position der ersten Reihe (neu) gesetzt (erste Position mit `typ === 'Sitzplatz'` in `sitzplan.reihen[0].positionen`...)"
  - Evidence: `buchung.ts` implements
    ```ts
    private ersteSitzplatzPosition(plan: Sitzplan): Position | null {
      for (const reihe of plan.reihen) {
        const position = reihe.positionen.find((p: SitzplanPosition) => p.typ === 'Sitzplatz');
        if (position) return { reihe: reihe.reihe, spalte: position.spalte };
      }
      return null;
    }
    ```
    instead of restricting the search to `plan.reihen[0]` as specified. In the common case (first row contains at least one `Sitzplatz` position) behavior is identical, but if the first row consisted entirely of `Gang` positions, the spec calls for `fokussiertePosition` to end up `null` (no initial roving-tabindex target on the first row), whereas the implementation silently falls through to the next row that has a `Sitzplatz` position. This is a functional divergence from the specified initialization rule, not merely a refactor — low real-world impact given typical seating-plan shapes, but it is a documented spec constraint that the code does not follow as written.

No other AC violations, missing behaviors, or contradictions between spec constraints and code were found. Minor non-issues checked and ruled out: the `viewChild` signal vs. `@ViewChild` decorator difference (explicitly justified in the Dev Agent's Completion Notes and functionally equivalent), and `buchung.scss` being listed in "Project Structure Notes" as a changed file but not touched in the diff (no styling change was actually needed there, so this is stale planning text rather than a code defect).

result: Acceptance audit of story 2.2 diff complete — one spec deviation found (`ersteSitzplatzPosition` in `seed-a-frontend/src/app/buchung/buchung.ts` scans all rows instead of only `reihen[0]` as Task 3 specifies), no AC violations otherwise.

